    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "B*Ai * / JAPAN AIR LINES\nSAFETY INSTRUCTIONS\nMAN TAKE-OFF AND LANDING\nBAGGAGE\nPlace baggage in the overhead bins or under a seat.\nPlease stow baggage securely.\n83.3\nFASTEN SEAT BELT TIGHT AND LOW Keep seat belt fastened whenever seated.\n#Lit\nTo fasten\nTo tighten\nTo unfasten\nSEAT POSITION\nTOILETTal\nSet seat back\nand table in\nupright position.\nNO SMOKING\nRefrain from\nsmoking in\nrestrooms or\naisles.\n*EA BRACE POSITIONS",
      "##0\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nUPPER DECK\n00D\n000000\nR\n0000000\nR\nA\n000000000000\n00000000000\n000000\n##0** FOR EVACUATION\nSi\nDo not carry any baggage.\nRemove highheeled shoes.\n000 0 0 0 0 2 0 0 000\nPut out cigarettes before evacuating.\nAfter evacuating, move away from the aircraft.\n3 6)\n*I DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT",
      "BAE/JAPAN AIR LINES\n7 LR\n141 sUD\nSAFETY INSTRUCTIONS\nHoARI LIFE VEST\nInflate when instructed by a crew member.\n2\n3\n4\nLife vest under seat.\n5\n6\n8\n*ФиТ.\nPull string to light emergency bea-\ncon.\nFor extra inflation blow into mouth\nhats\nTo Inflate.\npieces.\n*7#05A0XI TO FIT THE LIFE VEST TO A CHILD\n2\n3\nPass the straps between\nthe legs and secure\nin front.\n•*E*^FX**A*L**.Infant life vests provided by crew members.\nB*TXD OXYGEN MASK\nOxygen mask will appear automatically when needed.\nPut out your cigarette immediately. PULL\nAdults accompanied by small childlen should secure thier own mask first."
